docs/phase-1-plan.md:43:| 16 | `audit_events` | `kind` string, `actor` enum (human/system/agent), `user_id` (nullable), `subject` polymorphic (nullable), `data` jsonb, `reason`, `created_at` only. Postgres triggers reject UPDATE, DELETE, and TRUNCATE; `kind` is validated against `AuditEvent::KINDS`. Reserved for the PRD's "logged" list; not telemetry. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:56:## 2. Jobs (Solid Queue, `config/recurring.yml`, all times America/New_York)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:58:**Token model (revised after the step 4 counselors review).** Pause state is *derived* from the current token, never written by a failure. `schwab_tokens` gains `revoked_at`; `SchwabToken.current` is the newest by `issued_at, id`; `usable?` = present, not refresh-expired (`issued_at + 168.hours`, elapsed time not calendar days), not revoked. `SchwabToken.issue!(response)` inserts the new row and clears `system_settings.sync_paused_reason` in one transaction, enqueuing `Sync::CatchUpJob` after commit. `SchwabToken#refresh!` takes the row lock, reloads, and returns early if the row is no longer current or was refreshed in the last minute (so two workers cannot double-refresh and a stale row cannot act); it builds the client inside the lock; `access_expires_at` = now + `expires_in` − 60 s; `refresh_token` = response value or the existing one; `refresh_expires_at` is never touched. On `ReauthRequired` it sets `revoked_at` on the current row only, records `last_refresh_error` outside the lock so a rollback cannot lose it, audits `token_refresh_failed`, and sets `sync_paused_reason`. On `ServerError`/`TransportError` it records the error and does nothing else. `ensure_fresh!(margin:)` refreshes proactively when the access token is near expiry, so a 401 is the safety net rather than the norm. `Schwab.client` raises `Schwab::NoUsableToken` rather than letting nil reach a request.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:86:**Schwab client:** built to `docs/schwab-api-contract.md`. Net::HTTP; plaintext account numbers scrubbed inside the client before any body is returned; logs carry path templates (`/accounts/{hash}/orders`), never hashes, bodies, or headers; one time helper for the three input and three output formats; `BigDecimal` for every money and quantity value; a shared Solid Cache rate budget of 100 requests/minute across Puma and the worker; retries on 429, 5xx, and transport errors for GETs and the refresh grant only (1, 4, 16 s with jitter, `Retry-After` capped at 60 s), never on 4xx; one refresh-and-retry on a 401. Error classes: `AuthError`, `ReauthRequired`, `RateLimited`, `ServerError`, `RequestError`, `TransportError`, `UnknownOutcome` (non-idempotent calls only, chosen by HTTP method), `MappingError`. Interface adds `order(hash, order_id)` so working stops older than the lookback are re-fetched by id, and `instrument(symbol_or_cusip)` for identity fallback. Mappers return `Data` structs with a scrubbed `raw` member; jobs never see a Schwab field name. `Schwab::FakeClient` sits below the mappers and returns raw-shaped hashes with a scriptable per-call queue. Sync runs can finish `partial` with an `unmapped_values` count when individual records are quarantined.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:189:- App time zone `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`; Solid Queue recurring schedules use the same.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:196:2. Migrations 1–21, models with validations/enums, `AuditEvent` append-only trigger, `SystemSettings` singleton.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:25:| `Schwab::ReauthRequired < AuthError` | any token-endpoint 4xx (`invalid_client`, `invalid_grant`, `refresh_token_authentication_error`, `unsupported_token_type`); the pause path |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:26:| `Schwab::RateLimited` (`retry_after`) | 429 after the retry budget |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:27:| `Schwab::ServerError` | 5xx after retries |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:28:| `Schwab::RequestError` | 400, 403, 404; never retried; a 400 on `startDate` is how the lookback cap announces itself |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:30:| `Schwab::UnknownOutcome` | the same failures on a non-idempotent call (Phase 2 order POST); chosen by HTTP method so it can never be confused with the line above |
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:49:The refresh job runs every 25 minutes. A token-endpoint 4xx is `ReauthRequired`: no backoff, no retry, pause sync.
docs/schwab-api-contract.md:144:`Schwab::FakeClient` sits **below the mappers**: it returns scrubbed raw hashes in the same shape as the HTTP client, so seeds and Playwright exercise the mapping code where every shape assumption lives, and its fixtures double as the cassette-shaped fixtures for specs. It scripts auth too (`authorize_url`, `exchange_code`, `refresh`) and supports a per-call response queue so a test can say "first `orders` call raises RateLimited, second succeeds". Scenarios: re-auth success and failure, refresh expired, rate limited then success, server error then success, transport timeout, empty account, position removed between syncs, nested bracket child, transaction with missing CUSIP, unknown enum value, closed market day, quotes batch with one invalid symbol, and the four dashboard banner states.
